        "description": {
            "value": "<p>Roses go where you point them, and they are hungry.</p><p>Each target takes @Damage[(1+@item.level)d8[piercing]] damage plus @Damage[(@item.level)d6[persistent,bleed]] damage, with a basic Reflex save. A successful save negates the persistent bleed damage.</p><hr /><p><strong>Heightened (+1)</strong> The damage increases by 1d8 and the persistent bleed damage increases by 1d6.</p><hr /><p><strong>Tuning note:</strong> the guide gives this a 2d8 base and says it scales on the area spine, which puts it at 7d8 plus 6d6 persistent bleed against up to three creatures at rank 6 &mdash; for <em>one action</em>. That is above <em>Great Horn</em>, which costs two actions for 6d8 in a cone. It is implemented as written, but if Pisces plays out too strong, this is the number to cut: dropping the base to 1d8 brings it in line.</p>"
